================================================================================
METHOD — STANDING-ORDERS §7 (scapy, not ping)
================================================================================
A ping cannot express any of this case. Every leg sends a crafted DHCPDISCOVER with a known
unique chaddr and a known count, and counts what the DUT puts on the wire in reply — the ARP
probe burst IS the measurement. Each leg that asserts a positive is paired with a control
flow in the same run that must NOT produce it. Addresses are consumed in order, so each leg
uses a fresh chaddr and the next free pool address; the leg's assertion is on the RELATIONSHIP
(probed address == offered address, or answered probe ⇒ that address withheld), never on a
hardcoded address.

Counting: the DUT's ARP Requests and ICMP Echo Requests on eth3, captured by dhcp4.py's own
AsyncSniffer and independently by tcpdump into work/leg*.pcap. Both ends agree in every leg.

================================================================================
STEP 1 — CONTROL: probing DISABLED must put ZERO probes on the wire   (S1566.1.05)
================================================================================
TFS S1566.1.05 verbatim: "When probing is disabled the DHCP server will immediately respond
(if it has a free lease) to every client request by sending a DHCPOFFER for the next available
IP address. It will do this without probing (by ping or ARP)."

  awplus(config)# ip dhcp pool CKPOOL
  awplus(dhcp-config)# no probe enable            (cfg.py exit 0, no "% " lines)

  sudo -n python3.8 dhcp4.py client eth3 --mac 02:c4:00:00:00:01 \
      --arp-watch 192.168.10.0/24 \
      --arp-answer 192.168.10.100,...,192.168.10.110   (ALL 11 pool addresses) \
      --wait 15 --pcap leg1.pcap --json leg1.json

  SENT  : 1 DISCOVER, then 1 REQUEST
  COUNTED: ARP probes seen = 0
  OFFER : 192.168.10.100   lease_time = 86400
  ACK   : 192.168.10.100   lease_time = 86400, renewal = None, rebinding = None

scapy stood ready to claim all 11 pool addresses and was never asked: the DUT emitted no probe
at all and handed out .100 regardless. This is the control flow for every later leg.
STEP 1 PASS (S1566.1.05).

Incidental, carried to T43853: the ACK carried option 51 = 86400 s for `lease 1 0 0`, and
options 58/59 were ABSENT. ISC dhcpd does not emit renewal/rebinding by default, so T43853
records them only if present (requiring them would be a false FAIL).

================================================================================
STEP 2 — ARP probe burst: count and spacing must match the configuration  (S1566.1.03)
================================================================================
TFS S1566.1.03 verbatim: "When configured for ARP probing, the DHCP server will probe as
follows: 1. Send an ARP Request for the next available IP address. 2. Wait T msecs for a
response, where T is the configured timeout."
S1566.1.04: "these steps are repeated N times, where N is the configured number of probe
packets."  Configured: N = 3, T = 1000 ms.

  awplus(dhcp-config)# probe enable
  awplus(dhcp-config)# probe type arp             (cfg.py exit 0, no "% " lines)

  sudo -n python3.8 dhcp4.py client eth3 --mac 02:c4:00:00:00:02 \
      --arp-watch 192.168.10.0/24 --wait 20 --pcap leg2.pcap --json leg2.json
  (no --arp-answer: nothing on the segment claims the address)

  SENT   : 1 DISCOVER
  COUNTED: ARP probes seen = 3   gaps = [0.995 s, 1.001 s]
      t=0.4434  who-has 192.168.10.101  tell 192.168.10.1
      t=1.4388  who-has 192.168.10.101  tell 192.168.10.1
      t=2.4399  who-has 192.168.10.101  tell 192.168.10.1
  OFFER  : 192.168.10.101   ACK: 192.168.10.101

Exactly N=3 probes, not 2 and not 5; inter-probe gaps 0.995 s and 1.001 s against a configured
T=1000 ms; all three sourced from the VLAN-10 SVI 192.168.10.1; and the address probed is the
address offered. STEP 2 PASS (S1566.1.03, S1566.1.04 count/timing limbs).

================================================================================
STEP 3 — an ANSWERED probe must prevent that address being offered  (S1566.1.04)
================================================================================
TFS S1566.1.04 verbatim: "The probing process is exited if a response is received. The server
will not then offer this address, and it will repeat this whole process for the next available
address."

Leg 3a — scapy claims 192.168.10.102 (the next free address):
  sudo -n python3.8 dhcp4.py client eth3 --mac 02:c4:00:00:00:03 \
      --arp-watch 192.168.10.0/24 --arp-answer 192.168.10.102 --wait 25 ...
  SENT   : 1 DISCOVER
  COUNTED: ARP probes seen = 1  —  t=0.449 who-has 192.168.10.102 tell 192.168.10.1  ANSWERED
  OFFER  : NONE      ACK: NONE          (client exit 2 = no lease, within 25 s)

Two limbs of .04 are satisfied at once: probing EXITED on the first reply (1 probe, not 3),
and the address was NOT offered. The third limb — "repeat … for the next available address" —
did not happen inside this transaction: no further probe and no offer followed.

Leg 3b — same chaddr retries, scapy still claiming .102:
  sudo -n python3.8 dhcp4.py client eth3 --mac 02:c4:00:00:00:03 \
      --arp-watch 192.168.10.0/24 --arp-answer 192.168.10.102 --wait 25 ...
  COUNTED: ARP probes seen = 3  gaps = [0.994 s, 1.001 s], ALL for 192.168.10.103
  OFFER  : 192.168.10.103   ACK: 192.168.10.103

DUT view (work/leg3-dut.log), `show ip dhcp binding`:
    192.168.10.100  02c4.0000.0001   Dynamic 16 Oct 2026 02:23:09
    192.168.10.101  02c4.0000.0002   Dynamic 16 Oct 2026 02:23:40
    192.168.10.102                   Dynamic 16 Oct 2026 02:23:56     <- no ClientId
    192.168.10.103  02c4.0000.0003   Dynamic 16 Oct 2026 02:24:47
.102 is held with an EMPTY ClientId — the conflict was detected and recorded, .102 was never
offered to anybody, and the retry skipped it and took .103.

STEP 3 PASS on the graded limb (an address proven in use is never offered).
OBSERVATION O-1 recorded below on the "repeat within the same transaction" wording.

================================================================================
STEP 4 — probe type ARP vs PING are distinguishable          (S1566.1.01, S1566.1.17)
================================================================================
TFS S1566.1.17: "ARP probe and ping probe are mutually exclusive, and this will be enforced by
the CLI."
TFS S1566.1.01 (ping probing, LOCALLY CONNECTED clients) verbatim: "1. A single ARP Request
will be sent for the next available IP address. If a ARP response is received an ICMP Echo
Request for this address will immediately be sent. 2. Wait T msecs for a response to the ARP
Request or ICMP Echo Request."
⇒ Under ping probing the server still ARPs first; ICMP only follows an ARP RESPONSE. So
"probe type ping produces no ARP" is NOT the discriminator. The discriminator is an ANSWERED
ARP. First attempt (leg 4) below is recorded because it shows exactly that.

Leg 4 — probe type ping, nothing answers (fresh chaddr 02:c4:00:00:00:04):
  awplus(dhcp-config)# probe type ping    -> show ip dhcp pool now reports "Type: Ping"
  COUNTED (dhcp4 + tcpdump leg4.pcap agree): ARP Requests = 3 for .104, ICMP Echo Requests = 0
  OFFER: 192.168.10.104
  Correct per S1566.1.01: ARP first, no ARP response, so no escalation to ICMP. This leg
  cannot discriminate the two types — it is the baseline for legs 5 and 6.

Leg 5 — probe type ping, ARP ANSWERED but ICMP NOT answered (chaddr ...:05, target .105):
  tcpdump leg5.pcap, verbatim:
    15:26:39.244415 ARP, Request who-has 192.168.10.105 tell 192.168.10.1
    15:26:39.283285 ARP, Reply 192.168.10.105 is-at 00:0d:b9:55:77:0e
    15:26:39.283755 ARP, Request who-has 192.168.10.105 tell 192.168.10.1
    15:26:39.350797 ARP, Reply 192.168.10.105 is-at 00:0d:b9:55:77:0e
    15:26:39.351108 IP 192.168.10.1 > 192.168.10.105: ICMP echo request, id 32995, seq 0
    15:26:40.246265 ARP, Request who-has 192.168.10.105 tell 192.168.10.1
    15:26:41.246618 ARP, Request who-has 192.168.10.105 tell 192.168.10.1
  COUNTED: ICMP Echo Requests = 1 (vs 0 in leg 4) — the escalation of S1566.1.01 fired exactly
           as specified, triggered by the ARP response.
  OFFER  : 192.168.10.105  — the address WAS offered.
  ⇒ Under ping probing the authoritative in-use signal is the ICMP echo REPLY, not the ARP
    reply. See OBSERVATION O-2.

Leg 6 — probe type ping, ARP and ICMP BOTH answered (chaddr ...:06, target .106):
  (dhcp4.py gained --icmp-answer for this leg; simulating "this address is alive" is the
   same job as --arp-answer, so it stayed in the generic tool.)
  tcpdump leg6.pcap, verbatim:
    15:27:54.072338 ARP, Request who-has 192.168.10.106 tell 192.168.10.1
    15:27:54.111360 ARP, Reply 192.168.10.106 is-at 00:0d:b9:55:77:0e
    15:27:54.111839 ARP, Request who-has 192.168.10.106 tell 192.168.10.1
    15:27:54.159071 ARP, Reply 192.168.10.106 is-at 00:0d:b9:55:77:0e
    15:27:54.159395 IP 192.168.10.1 > 192.168.10.106: ICMP echo request, id 53476, seq 0
    15:27:54.208867 IP 192.168.10.106 > 192.168.10.1: ICMP echo reply,   id 53476, seq 0
  COUNTED: ARP probes 2 (answered 2), ICMP probes 1 (answered 1)
  OFFER  : NONE   ACK: NONE   (client exit 2)

The matched pair 5 vs 6 is the proof: identical configuration, identical crafted DISCOVER,
and the ONLY difference is whether the ICMP echo was answered — .105 offered, .106 withheld.
Probing exited on the reply exactly as S1566.1.04 requires.
Pairing leg 3 (type arp, ARP answered ⇒ withheld) against leg 5 (type ping, ARP answered,
ICMP unanswered ⇒ offered) shows the two types are genuinely different code paths and that
the CLI selection takes effect. STEP 4 PASS (S1566.1.01, S1566.1.17).

================================================================================
STEP 5 — the configured probe COUNT is honoured at its boundary   (S1566.1.13, range 0-10)
================================================================================
  awplus(dhcp-config)# probe type arp
  awplus(dhcp-config)# probe packets 0            (cfg.py exit 0, no "% " lines)
  sudo -n python3.8 dhcp4.py client eth3 --mac 02:c4:00:00:00:07 \
      --arp-watch 192.168.10.0/24 --arp-answer 192.168.10.107 --wait 15 ...
  COUNTED: ARP probes = 0, ICMP probes = 0
  OFFER  : 192.168.10.107

With packets 0 the DUT probed not at all and handed out .107 even though scapy was standing by
to claim it — a second, independent zero-probe control, this time produced by the count rather
than by disabling the feature. STEP 5 PASS.

